CommitDate: Sat Nov 7 14:48:36 2026 +0000

    Harden verification artifacts; stop claiming cryptographic independence
    
    Second independent review of 591bb09 found that a self-written artifact cannot
    prove independent verification on this host (all offices share one uid), and
    that the check had real bypasses. This commit addresses the mechanical defects
    and states the honest limit instead of overclaiming.
    
    Hardening:
      * verified_at must satisfy first_seen < verified_at <= now and
        last_seen <= verified_at (no pre-dated, no future-dated, no stale artifact
        surviving a relapse);
      * evidence.ref must be a relative path inside the state root, with no ".."
        and no symlink on any component, and must be a regular file within a
        4 MiB cap (blocks absolute paths, traversal, symlink escape and /dev/zero);
      * timestamps require type(x) is int (JSON true is not a timestamp);
      * read() tolerates OSError, so an unreadable or directory-valued state file
        can no longer abort the whole reconcile pass;
      * closure_evidence records provenance as
        "declared_by_artifact_content_not_cryptographically_enforced" so no reader
        mistakes the artifact for a signature.
    
    Routing:
      * branch-health emits case_awaiting_verification when any open case has
        awaiting_independent_verification, so a cleared symptom without
        verification is not reported healthy; the reconciler treats it as an
        advisory META signal and never creates a case from it;
      * the Clerk sitting prompt no longer says closure follows "repeated
        deterministic observation"; it states the artifact requirement.
    
    Tests: rejection cases now assert the counts are preserved and the flag is set;
    add absolute-path, traversal, symlink, boolean-timestamp and future-timestamp
    refusals; assert a matching artifact cannot substitute for a missing continuity
    receipt; assert the advisory signal is emitted and not turned into a case.
    
    Not claimed: that this proves who wrote the artifact. Honest limit is in the
    docstring, closure_evidence and this message. Earlier closures made under the
    rejected probe-count rule are left as historical records, not silently
    re-labelled or reopened.

